<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-VON GRUENIGEN WINS MEN'S GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-VON GRUENIGEN WINS MEN'S GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Von Gruenigen of Switzerland won the men's giant slalom gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Wednesday in a total time of two minutes 48.23 seconds, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Lasse Kjus of Norway took the silver in 2:49.35 and Andreas Schifferer of Austria was third in 2:49.68.</p>
